laurel 2720: calendar from the PM6125 RTC + USB settime (lock screen showed "Wednesday, December 31" ~4 PM = epoch 0 in PST; usblog "settime: error: unknown command"). Port of negroni 0203/0212 onto the topaz platform expert. New bsd/dev/laurel_rtc.c: SweetPlatformExpert::getUTCTimeOfDay/setUTCTimeOfDay -> RTC_RW at PM6125 SID 0 0x6000 (pm6125.dtsi qcom,qpnp-rtc; 4.14 qpnp-rtc.c: subtype 0x6005=0x01, ctrl 0x6046 bit 7, seconds 0x6048..0x604b LE, re-read byte 0 on carry) through the one SPMI core (sweet_spmi.c, new user SWEET_SPMI_RTC, reads only). DT qcom,qpnp-rtc-write=<0> and Android keeps the wall offset in time_daemon (/data/vendor/time, gone with the Android userdata): the PMIC is never written; wall = counter + own offset saved in /private/var/db/laurel_rtc (bsd_init after the root mount; thread-call writer, retries while the root is read-only); a counter already in 2020..2100 is used as it is; floor = build date - 1 day. USB ctl `settime <s>[.<frac>]` (any context: queued, applied by ud_thread within 1 ms, or taken at the calendar start when it came first) and `time`; early (raw) mode too. Self-check: SPMI core, channel, subtype, enable bit, counter read; else one `LAUREL RTC: off: <why>` line. Kill switch laurelrtc=0. The IOStartIOKit line of 2000 is now `LAUREL IORTC:`. Lines: `LAUREL RTC: on: <date> (raw N, ...)` or `LAUREL RTC: off: counter N s (...) is not wall time ...`, `LAUREL CTL: settime S.U: clock set (...)`, `LAUREL RTC: saved offset ...`. Details: docs/laurel_sprout/rtc-statusbar.md.

